=== probe rounds (L7TacticProbe.lean, untracked, 3 one-shot runs) ===
Run A (352 s): the ZMod shapes that fail in the lane's context CLOSE in isolation
  (`ring` on `-x + -x = -(x*2)`, `(3 : ZMod n) + -3 = 0`, `((4 : ZMod n) - 1)`
  numerals). So the failures are context-sensitive in `ZMod n` with a variable
  modulus — the lane's mixed statement-/proof-side `ZMod n` terms.
Run B (345 s): with `[Fact (Nat.Prime n)]` as a theorem BINDER `ring` fails on
  `-x + x = 0`, `-x - x = -(2*x)`, numerals, and `rw [Odd.neg_pow _]` fails to
  match — while the same code with the instance introduced in-proof passes.
  Reproducible environment fact; documented in MATHLIB_API_LESSONS.md.
Run C (345 s, ℤ toolbox): whole `Int.ModEq` API (.pow/.add/.mul/.neg/.add_right/
  .add_left/.trans/.symm/refl), ZMod→ℤ bridges, `Int.Prime.dvd_mul'`/`dvd_pow'`,
  ℤ FLT via `L5.L5_gcd_eq_one_of_not_dvd` — all green. The one failure was a
  `have hid : <numeral identity> = 3` whose type DEFAULTED TO ℕ (truncated
  subtraction ⇒ false identity); with `… : ℤ` pinned it closes. This drove the
  decision to carry S3-S5 in ℤ congruence form.

